1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Can day-seven physiology forecast the day-twelve endpoint for an unseen chemical—
and can the system refuse when the forecast is unsafe?

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The demo uses precomputed held-out evidence. OBSERVED shows early measurements.
PREDICTED shows the later forecast and calibrated interval.
HYPOTHESIS marks claims not validated by this study.

3
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The study has 136 chemicals and about 4,200 trajectories.
All five endpoints improved by 14.2 to 39.0 percent versus a strong inner-selected baseline, BT+,
and by 12.3 to 42.9 percent versus the stricter BT++.
Every paired chemical-level 95 percent confidence interval excluded zero.

4
00:01:30,000 --> 00:02:05,000
A registered negative control stopped the pipeline.
The bounded audit found no future-derived feature or alignment defect,
and the failure remains visible.

5
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Nominal 90% intervals achieved 91.0% to 92.4% empirical coverage.
Abstention passed on three of five endpoints; the other two remain limitations.

6
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:20,000
For accepted cases, DIV7 forecasts are available five days before DIV12.
DIV7 physiology is the dominant predictive family; this is not a causal claim.

7
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:50,000
The demo shows a representative correct case and a disclosed failure case.
The interval and abstention decision remain visible in both.

8
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Predictive value was retained under a held-out NTP↔ToxCast cohort shift
without model retuning. This is not external laboratory or device transfer.

9
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:35,000
This is rat cortical neural MEA data, not organ-on-chip data.
A new platform requires local validation and recalibration.

10
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Forecast when evidence is strong; continue the assay when it is not.
Research decision support—not autonomous assay termination.
